petra 0

# A hoist hook rated by proof testing. The lift load is known only by its range and
# its mean from the duty log, so the overload claim uses R5: over every distribution on
# [0, 40] kN with mean 10 kN, P(load > capacity) <= 10 / 36 < 3/10 at the lowest
# capacity, with no distribution assumed. The proof tests give a second, empirical
# claim through R6: 300 trials, 0 failures, so (1 - 1/100)^300 ~ 0.049 <= 1 - 0.95.
# The demand domain knows no bolt: the capacity is a measured input. Expected: PASS.

demand hook {
  capacity given capacity
}
